Version 4.0.0
    - Major version bump to match pydivert 4.0.0.
    - Linux support (experimental; x86_64/aarch64) via the bundled eBPFDivert 0.0.5 (libebpfdivert.so), an eBPF implementation of the WinDivert API. Requires kernel 5.10+ with BTF and glibc 2.28+; cgroup v2 for the FLOW/SOCKET layers.
    - Filters are compiled and evaluated by WinDivert's own filter engine on Linux too; all layers are supported.
    - JNA and Project Panama adapters for Linux; the 80-byte WINDIVERT_ADDRESS round-trips intact between recv and send.
    - Linux-only system properties: jdivert.ebpf.interfaces and jdivert.ebpf.ringBytes.
    - On Linux, WinDivertException carries errno values (e.g. EINVAL 22 for a bad filter).
    - Native libraries are extracted to a per-user, versioned directory (mode 0700 on Linux).
    - New API: stream() and PacketBuilder. Async calls run on virtual threads on Java 21+.
    - Packet.parse skips event layers and short buffers.

Version 3.0.0
    - Major version bump to match pydivert 3.0.0.
    - Bundle WinDivert 2.2.2 (64-bit).
    - Updated for modern Windows environments (10/11).
    - Support for new layers (FLOW, SOCKET, REFLECT).
    - Added Vagrantfile for Windows testing.
    - Security policy (SECURITY.md) added.
    - Dual-licensed under GPLv2 and LGPLv3.
    - Implement payload resizing in Packet.setPayload.
    - Make WinDivert implement AutoCloseable for try-with-resources.
    - Improved test robustness and timeouts.
    - Fixed memory issues in Vagrant VM by increasing WinRM limits.
    - Fixed build failure on Java 25 by updating JaCoCo to 0.8.14.
    - Improved code coverage reporting for Multi-Release JAR by refining JaCoCo exclusions and ensuring tests use the Panama implementation on Java 22+.
    - Fixed Panama coverage on Java 25 by correctly configuring the test classpath and adding required JVM flags.
    - Centralized all Maven plugin versions in pom.xml properties.

Version 1.1
    - Initial support for WinDivert 1.4.

Version 1.0
    - Initial release.
